[What is a preference center?](https://www.braze.com/resources/articles/preference-center): A preference center is a page on a brand's app or website where customers control which messages they get (across email, push, SMS, and other channels) instead of facing a single all-or-nothing unsubscribe choice. It lets users tell a brand exactly what channels, topics, and frequency they're willing to receive, which keeps more of them reachable over time.

[What should a preference center include?](https://www.braze.com/resources/articles/preference-center): A preference center should include: Channel choices – options to opt in/out of email, push, SMS, in-app messages, etc. separately Topic or content categories – e.g., promotions vs. product updates vs. account/service notices (in Braze, these map to Subscription Groups) Frequency controls – how often a user wants to hear from you Simplicity – the article specifically warns against overwhelming users with too many choices; a handful of clear options works better than an exhaustive list Easy access, not just onboarding – it should be revisitable any time, not a one-time setup step, since periodic check-ins build trust A branded, on-platform look – it's worth customizing the design so it feels like a natural part of your product rather than a bare settings form Genuine follow-through – whatever preferences a user sets need to actually be respected in your sending logic, or the whole exercise is pointless

[What is an email preference center vs. an unsubscribe page?](https://www.braze.com/resources/articles/preference-center): An unsubscribe page is binary: The user leaves your list entirely, and you lose the ability to message them at all. An email preference center gives granular control instead: rather than turning email off completely, a user can narrow down to just the newsletters or categories they care about (e.g., deals but not product announcements). The brand keeps a communication channel open at a lower volume rather than losing it altogether.

[How preference centers reduce churn?](https://www.braze.com/resources/articles/preference-center): By letting users self-select relevant content and frequency from the start, brands avoid the fatigue that drives full opt-outs, protect deliverability, and end up with a smaller but more engaged and durable list of reachable customers, rather than risking losing users altogether.

